## 2. In API Logic Hunting & BOLA: Set Theory & Relations
Broken Object Level Authorization (BOLA/IDOR) occurs when an application fails to check user access permissions accurately. This is purely a failure of Sets and Relations. [2] 

* The Concept: Think of User A's accessible objects as Set A, and User B's objects as Set B. A secure system must enforce that the intersection of these sets satisfies strict relational rules.
* The Math in Action:
* You can map out authorization matrices using Cartesian Products (matching all user roles against all API actions).
   * By systematically testing the boundaries of these mathematical relations (e.g., testing if an application's permission inheritance is truly transitive), you can find flaws where a low-privilege user can access a high-privilege object set.

