## 4. In High-Impact Bug Classes (SSRF & RCE): Boolean Algebra & Automata Theory
Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) and Remote Code Execution (RCE) usually involve bypassing Input Validation Filters (like Web Application Firewalls or Regex matching systems). [7] 

* The Concept: Firewalls and filters are built using regular expressions and string matching, which are derived directly from Automata Theory (Formal Languages) and Boolean Algebra. [8] 
* The Math in Action:
* When a developer creates a blacklist filter (e.g., "Block strings containing 169.254.169.254 or admin"), they are creating a Boolean logic gate.
   * You can use De Morgan’s Laws and equivalent logical transformations to rewrite your payloads into alternative, structurally identical expressions that the Boolean logic of the firewall fails to catch, but the backend interpreter executes perfectly (such as converting IP addresses to Hexadecimal, Octal, or Dword formats).

